# Edge cases and clarity (Required)

Ekum hits many client bugs from **unspoken exceptions** (e.g. Connection bypassing look-only; unfollow notifying the wrong hop; Place not checking buyer follow). When developing or expanding a feature:

## Before coding

1. Name **who** (supplier / trader / buyer), **which grant** (See / Repost-Pack / Connection / Direct Link / allowForward / audience), and **which surface** (Explore Repost, shop Share/Forward, Place, chat system line).
2. Walk **revoke and empty hops**: Pack → look; unfollow; no thread; look-only + Connected; Everyone vs Followers; mixed members.
3. If product copy uses the same word for two jobs (**Share** vs **Repost** vs **Forward**), say so and lock which gate applies.
4. **Ask the user** when an edge is unclear — do not invent a silent bypass (especially Connection unlocking a grant).

## While implementing

- Prefer **one enforcement path** (API ceiling + UI that reads the same check). Dual `pathForPair` copies must stay in sync.
- Notify only the party who needs to act; do not leak trader-only concepts (Direct Link) to mill/buyer in shared chat unless product says so.
- List chrome vs Place eligibility can differ — document both (e.g. gray CTA mill-only; Place also needs buyer follow).

## In the reply to the user

Call out explicitly:

- **Edge cases covered** (short list).
- **Fixes or clarity still needed** — open product questions, deferred Later items, or known holes (do not bury in Completeness only).
- Anything that **conflicts** with an older Completeness rule (mark Redesign).

Green tests are not enough if a revoke hop or naming collision was never considered.
